Its arm V drives scripts/validate-fixture-git-env.sh, which is a DISTRIBUTION-ONLY
validator: its population is core/fixtures/*/run.sh, a path that does not exist on a
consumer, where the same program refuses with exit 2 (measured on a tree built by
install.sh). Shipped, this fixture would report on a subject the consumer does not
have. The SEAM it guards does ship -- core/fixtures/lib/ carries no marker -- and a
consumer exercises it through its own copies of the 27 fixtures that source it.
